Portions derived from Ultimate CA Manager (UCM) by the same author,
relicensed under Apache-2.0 for inclusion in this project:
  - frontend design system (CSS tokens, Tailwind configuration, theme
    context, fonts, base UI components, application shell and layout)
  - backend patterns for session authentication, CSRF handling, rate
    limiting and secret encryption at rest
  - web certificates (backend/pelagos/core/webcert): the ACME client (JWS
    signing, external account binding, orders, DNS-01 and HTTP-01), the
    extensible DNS provider layout with the Hetzner provider, certificate,
    PKCS#12 and chain parsing and ordering, pre-install checks, and the
    calls of UCM's REST API v2 (CSR upload and signing, export, revocation)
  - security keys and passkeys (backend/pelagos/auth/webauthn.py,
    backend/pelagos/auth/twofa.py, backend/pelagos/services/webauthn_service.py):
    the WebAuthn ceremonies over py_webauthn, the signature counter rule and
    the second factor enforcement policy

